Transposition is the cipher and that is exactly how 5,000 items ended up being recovered from King Tuts tomb.  I really employ you to read about this topic its really fascinating.  They found iron daggers on the mummy which smelting wasn't discovered until 800 years after King Tut, the sarcophagus' (4 inside of each other like Russian dolls) have been reused from other tombs and places, and all of the items are from other periods and places in Egypt's history.   Theres a few good Nat Geo documentaries on Disney+.  Its more interesting than you think... but you really have to build a timeline of events not just in the discovery of the tomb and how it was excavated but a broader picture of what was going in with Egypt during this time.  At the very same time this happened Egypt became an independent country and they needed to create a strong cultural identity (and they did).

But transposition, taking something from one place and putting in another.

